  "id": "sampling-and-surveys",
  "version": "1.0.0",
  "status": "draft",
  "subject": "Sampling and survey design: how data are collected from a population, and what can go wrong",
  "outOfScope": [
    "Sampling distributions, standard errors, margins of error and confidence intervals (the next pack); this pack only says that a margin of error does not measure bias",
    "Sample-size formulas and how to choose a sample size",
    "The mathematics of survey estimators: expansion, ratio and Hansen-Hurwitz estimators, optimal allocation, design effects and variance formulas",
    "Randomisation and experimental design in depth (see the A/B testing pack); this pack names observational studies and experiments and the difference between them",
    "Probability, random variables and the binomial distribution (see the Probability distributions pack)",
    "Snowball and respondent-driven sampling of hidden populations",
    "Weighting methods in detail, such as raking algorithms, propensity models, matching and multilevel regression and poststratification",
    "Polling methodology for specific elections, and forecasting election results",
    "Survey tooling such as Qualtrics, SurveyMonkey and Google Forms"
  ],
